dts: rk3576: clock the GPU from SCMI so the top OPPs are reachable

The GPU OPP table lists 700, 800, 900 and 950 MHz, but panfrost drives
CLK_GPU, a divider off GPLL/CPLL/AUPLL/SPLL/LPLL. None of those produce
those rates, so the clock framework rounds down and the hardware silently
runs slower than the OPP says. Measured on an ArmSoM Sige5:

  requested   actual
    300 MHz   297 MHz
    400 MHz   396 MHz
    500 MHz   500 MHz
    600 MHz   594 MHz
    700 MHz   594 MHz
    800 MHz   786 MHz
    900 MHz   786 MHz
    950 MHz   786 MHz

So the top three OPPs all deliver 786 MHz, and devfreq, the energy model
and the thermal governor all believe the GPU is at 950 MHz while it runs
17% slower. Rates above the PVTPLL threshold are only reachable through
SCMI: BL31 owns the GPU PVTPLL and switches between the normal PLL and
PVTPLL on an SCMI rate request.

Make SCMI_CLK_GPU the clock panfrost scales. PCLK_GPU_ROOT comes along as
"bus" so panfrost keeps it enabled: BL31 programs PVTPLL through registers
in the GPU block reached over that APB clock, and it does not enable the
clock itself. The rk3528 GPU binding uses the same SCMI-as-core pattern.

Mark the 300 MHz OPP opp-suspend so the normal PLL is selected before the
GPU is runtime suspended, as rk3528 does - suspending while on PVTPLL
hangs the SoC.

Drop the 950 MHz OPP. Table 3-2 of the RK3576 datasheet (rev 1.5) gives a
900 MHz maximum for the GPU, against 950 MHz for the NPU. The rate was
unreachable over the CRU, so this series would be the first time it could
actually be applied.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
@@ -350,6 +350,7 @@
 		opp-300000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <700000 700000 850000>;
+			opp-suspend;
 		};
 
 		opp-400000000 {
@@ -380,11 +381,6 @@
 		opp-900000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <900000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <825000 825000 850000>;
-		};
-
-		opp-950000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <950000000>;
-			opp-microvolt = <850000 850000 850000>;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -1270,8 +1266,8 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x27800000 0x0 0x20000>;
 			assigned-clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_GPU>;
 			assigned-clock-rates = <198000000>;
-			clocks = <&cru CLK_GPU>;
-			clock-names = "core";
+			clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_GPU>, <&cru PCLK_GPU_ROOT>;
+			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			dynamic-power-coefficient = <1625>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 347 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				     <GIC_SPI 348 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
